course: dictionary
lesson: 6120
title: Mid: the middle, or just average
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Mid is a small word with two main jobs. Put it in front of a word, often with a hyphen, and it means in the middle of something: «mid-morning» is the middle part of the morning, and «mid-air» is the middle of the air. Look at the words around it to see which meaning fits.
explain: Some phrases show something happening halfway through. A sentence that stops in the middle is cut off «mid-sentence». The word mid tells you the action was interrupted, not finished.
explain: Slang works differently. «That film was mid.» Mid here means just average, not very good. Jake says chess is «mid», which means boring and nothing special. Test it: swap in just average, and if the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
explain: In old poems you may find mid on its own. It is a short form of amid, which means among. Context still helps: if the words around it describe a crowd or a group, then mid probably means among.
fact: Mid means in the middle of something.
fact: Mid is often joined to another word with a hyphen: mid-morning, mid-air, mid-sentence.
fact: In US slang, «mid» means just average or not very good.
fact: In maths, the midpoint is the point exactly halfway along a line.
fact: Mid is short for amid, which means among, and it is used mostly in poems.
exercise: What does mid mean in «That film was mid.»? | Very exciting | Very long | In the middle of the film | *Just average, not very good
exercise: What does mid mean in «mid-morning»? | *In the middle of the morning | Very early in the morning, before breakfast | At the very start of the night | Not at all
exercise: What does «mid-air» mean? | Under the ground | *Halfway up in the air, in the middle of the air | Very cold and windy | Covered in mud
test: Jake says chess is «mid». What does he mean? | Very exciting | Very wet | Very old | *Boring, nothing special
test: In an old poem you read «mid the trees». What does mid mean? | Middle of the sea | Very old | *Among | Wet and muddy
exam: Which use of mid means halfway through something? | Just average, as in «That film was mid.» | Boring, as in Jake's chess club | *Interrupted halfway, as in «mid-sentence» | Among, as in an old poem
